Yleaf-derived Y-DNA analysis
==========================

src/wgsextract_cli/ydna/yleaf_native contains modified code derived from
Yleaf v4.1.6, https://github.com/genid/Yleaf, commit
c167c4e8951623a53c370e7c300a0cfc7f411b62.

Yleaf was developed at the Department of Genetic Identification, Erasmus MC
University Medical Centre Rotterdam, The Netherlands, by Arwin Ralf,
Diego Montiel Gonzalez, Kaiyin Zhong and Manfred Kayser. The prediction/tree
implementation credits Bram van Wersch; Yleaf.py credits Diego Montiel
Gonzalez and extensive modifications by Bram van Wersch.

The original source headers license these files under GNU GPL version 3 or
later. WGS Extract's modifications and distribution retain that license;
the complete GPL v3 text is in LICENSE. Per-file headers identify the source
files and modifications. Yleaf data is distributed separately, unmodified,
with upstream provenance and SHA-256 checksums in the yleaf-data release
manifest (release tags: yleaf-data-v<VERSION>).

Those Yleaf data packs hold third-party data under its own terms, not the GPL:
the hg19 and t2t packs include UCSC's hg38ToHg19.over.chain.gz and
hg38ToHs1.over.chain.gz, which UCSC licenses free for non-commercial use by
independent researchers and nonprofit organizations only; UCSC's liftOver
README, which must accompany them, is
src/wgsextract_cli/ydna/yleaf_native/UCSC-liftOver-README.txt and is installed
beside each chain. The packs' FamilyTreeDNA and ISOGG tree tables come from
Yleaf's data release; neither source publishes a licence for them (see
trees.json "terms").

The default YFull Y tree is not part of WGS Extract either. It is downloaded
on demand as two separately licensed data modules (release tags:
yleaf-yfull-v<VERSION>): yfull-tree (YFull YTree, CC-BY-4.0) and
yfull-ybrowse-positions (marker positions derived from YBrowse, CC-BY-SA
Thomas Krahn YSEQ (2022), no CC-BY-SA version stated). Each module carries its own licence file and
SHA-256 pins; neither licence applies to this program.

Please cite:
Ralf A, Montiel González D, Zhong K, Kayser M. Yleaf: Software for Human
Y-Chromosomal Haplogroup Inference from Next-Generation Sequencing Data.
Molecular Biology and Evolution 35(5):1291-1294 (2018).
https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy032

The native adapter replaces Yleaf's CLI, process globals and pandas tables
with a typed library interface, existing samtools/bcftools integration,
verified lazy data downloads, deterministic marker presentation and result
provenance. Prediction rules and marker/QC filtering derive from upstream.
These modifications were made by WGS Extract contributors on 2026-11-01.
This project is independent and is not endorsed by the Yleaf authors.

CPIC content
============

src/wgsextract_cli/assets/report/pgx_context_rules.json quotes recommendation
text from the Clinical Pharmacogenetics Implementation Consortium (CPIC®)
database, release v1.61.0, which CPIC dedicates to the public domain under
CC0 1.0 (https://github.com/cpicpgx/cpic-data/blob/v1.61.0/LICENSE.md). The
database itself is not distributed with WGS Extract: `report --pgx-context
--download` fetches the SHA-256-pinned export from files.cpicpgx.org. As CPIC
requests, the report credits CPIC (primary source www.clinpgx.org), cites each
guideline's publication and the release, and notes that CPIC guidelines are
updated over time. CPIC® is a registered service mark of the US Department of
Health & Human Services; WGS Extract is not endorsed by CPIC.
